**How the swap works.** VS Code cannot change a view container's icon at run time (it is fixed in the manifest). So: two view containers, one per icon, adjacent in `contributes.viewsContainers`, each holding the eggzibit view with a `when` on a context key `eggzibit.hasPages` (true in one, false in the other) that the extension sets from the store and updates on change; VS Code hides a container whose views are all hidden. Known costs, to check and report: each container keeps its own position (a user who drags one must drag the other), and an open view may close when the first page arrives — if the swap is jarring in practice, say so on the ticket before shipping (the alternative is one icon with a count badge).

