Done in lap session S200, git 9dae342.

**What changed.** `hist_clear_tmp`, which every writer runs under the lock right after opening (including `lap rebuild`), now removes:
- temp files in `.lap/log/` (as before);
- temp files directly in `.lap/`, where chunk temps are written since T-142;
- temp files at any depth of `.lap/shadow/`;
- `log.converting/` and `log.replaced/`, whenever no single-file `log.jsonl` is left. The conversion itself has either finished or failed the open by then, so nothing there is still needed.

Under the lock every `*.tmp.<pid>` is a leftover, so all of them go. There's no pid check, as the ticket allowed. The shadow walk costs one directory walk per write (this repository: 524 shadow files).

**Tests**: unit 4607 passed (new: a chunk temp in `.lap/`, a nested shadow temp, and both conversion folders are removed; the shadow file and the history stay). e2e 175 passed. The new scenario hand-makes all four leftovers; they are gone after one commit, and again after `lap rebuild`, and `verify --deep` stays clean. Checked against the pre-change hist.c: all 8 checks fail there.
